  "title": "Qt: Parent the QColorDialog in ColoringRulesDialog",
  "description": "On Linux (at least Wayland + GTK3), a Qt applicationModal dialog is\nnot necessarily always-on-top on the application. If parented, it\nis always on top of the parent.\n\nParent the QColorDialog, which at least makes it stay on top of\nthe ColoringRulesDialog. ColoringRulesDialog itself, like other\nApplicationModal GeometryStateDialogs, also ought to stay on top\nof the application, but we intentionally don't parent GSDs on\nLinux (or Windows) because that makes them always-on-top even\nwhen not modal.\n\nPart of #19099. The issue for the modal GeometryStateDialogs\nin general, including the ColoringRulesDialog, needs more work.",
